## Suggested Fix

Mirror the `ScriptArray.Multiply` hardening in `ScriptRange.Multiply`: charge the outer repetition against `LoopLimit` independently of inner emission. Minimal change — call `context.StepLoop` once per outer iteration (before the inner `foreach`) so `count` repetitions are themselves bounded:

```csharp
int loopStep = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < count; i++)
{
    context.StepLoop(span, ref loopStep, loopType);  // charge the repetition itself
    foreach (var value in left)
    {
        context.StepLoop(span, ref loopStep, loopType);
        yield return value;
    }
}
```

